# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/

# Turborepo cache
.turbo/

# Generated Prisma clients (regenerate with `prisma generate`)
**/src/generated/

# Environment files — these hold database credentials
#
# The negation has to cover the same family the rule above it does. `.env.*`
# ignores `.env.ticketing.example` as readily as `.env.ticketing`, and
# `!.env.example` only rescues the exact name — so an example file for any
# variant is silently untracked, and the person who wrote it has no reason to
# look. Nothing depends on that today; the trap is that `git add` would appear
# to work and commit nothing.
#
# Same shape as the .dockerignore bug this PR fixes, which is why both are here:
# a rule matching one exact name where the repository has a family.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# JWT signing keys — NEVER commit these
**/keys/
*.pem

# Logs and OS noise
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
